.TH "easel compalign" 1 "@EASEL_DATE@" "Easel @EASEL_VERSION@" "Easel Manual"

.SH NAME
easel compalign \- compare trusted vs. test multiple sequence alignments

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B easel compalign
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I trusted_msafile
.I test_msafile



.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
.B easel compalign
evaluates the accuracy of a predicted multiple sequence alignment with
respect to a trusted alignment of the same sequences. 

.PP
Both MSA files must be in Stockholm format and contain 'reference'
annotation, which appears as "#=GC RF" per-column markup for each MSA.
The trusted and test MSA files must contain the same number of MSAs
(if there is more than one) and in the same order. Each predicted MSA
in the
.I test_msafile 
is compared against the corresponding trusted MSA from the
.I trusted_msafile.
Each corresponding trusted and test
MSA pair must contain the same sequences (i.e. if they were
unaligned they would be identical) in the same order in both
MSAs. Further,
the number of consensus columns marked by
the reference (RF) annotation must be the same
in each trusted/test MSA pair.

.PP
.B easel compalign
compares MSAs based on their annotated consensus columns (reference
annotation).  The number of correctly predicted residues for each
sequence is computed as follows. A residue that is in the Nth consensus
column (i.e. nongap RF annotation) in the trusted alignment must also
appear in the Nth consensus
column in the predicted alignment to be counted as 'correct',
otherwise it is 'incorrect'. A residue that appears in a nonconsensus column
(an insertion relative to consensus; marked with a gap symbol in RF annotation)
in the trusted alignment between consensus columns N and N+1 must also
appear in the nonconsensus insertion columns between consensus
columns N and N+1 to be counted as 'correct', otherwise it is
incorrect.

.PP
Aside from putting inserted residues in the right insertion position
(defined by two flanking consensus columns), insertions are otherwise
treated as unaligned, as is the convention for profile HMMs and SCFGs
(HMMER and Infernal, for example).

.PP
The default output of
.B easel compalign
lists each sequence and the number of correctly and incorrectly
aligned residues for that sequence. These counts are broken down into
counts for residues in the predicted alignments that occur in
annotated consensus 'match' columns and nonconsensus 'insert'
columns. A 'match' column is one for which the RF annotation does not
contain a gap. An 'insert' column is one for which the RF annotation
does contain a gap.


.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-h
Print brief help; includes version number and summary of
all options.

.TP
.B \-c
Print per-column statistics instead of per-sequence statistics.

.TP
.B \-p 
Print statistics on accuracy versus posterior probability
values. Every
sequence in the 
.I test_msafile
must be annotated with posterior probabilities (#=GR <seqname> PP) for this
option to work.


.SH EXPERT OPTIONS

.TP
.BI \-\-p\-mask " <f>"
This option may only be used in combination with the 
.B \-p
option. Read a "mask" from file 
.IR <f> .
The mask file must consist of a single line, of only '0' and '1'
characters. There must be exactly RFLEN characters where RFLEN is the
number of consensus columns (nongap characters in the RF annotation) of all alignments in
both 
.I trusted_msafile
and
.IR test_msafile .
Positions of the mask that are '1' characters indicate that the
corresponding nongap RF position is included by the mask. The
posterior probability accuracy statistics for match columns will only
pertain to positions that are included by the mask, those that are
excluded will be ignored from the accuracy calculation.

.TP
.BI \-\-c2dfile " <f>"
Save a 'draw file' to file 
.I <f>
which can be read into the 
.B easel ssdraw
miniapp. This draw file will define two postscript pages for 
.BR "easel ssdraw" .
The first page will depict the frequency of errors per match position and
frequency of gaps per match position, indicated by magenta and yellow,
respectively. The darker magenta, the more errors and the darker
yellow, the more gaps. The second page will depict the frequency of
errors in insert positions in shades of magenta, the darker the
magenta the more errors in inserts after each position. See
.B easel ssdraw
documentation for more information on these diagrams. 
Requires the
.B -c
option.

.TP
.B \-\-amino
Assert that 
.I trusted_msafile
and 
.I test_msafile
contain protein sequences. 

.TP 
.B \-\-dna
Assert that 
.I trusted_msafile
and 
.I test_msafile
contain DNA sequences. 

.TP 
.B \-\-rna
Assert that 
.I trusted_msafile
and 
.I test_msafile
contain RNA sequences. 



.SH SEE ALSO

.B man easel
for more information about 
Easel miniapps, their shared behaviors, and 
some standardized options.

